1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:01:58,860
Part 11 stopped on the sentence of the missing person. If a relative of the house is lost, they put out a notice. This is his picture. This is his nature. If anyone tells, they will give a reward. I did not like that they kept a dog. Once I said, why have you kept this. Then, suddenly, their dog left the house one day, and no one knew where it had gone. This was when I was in India. I went there, and they were pasting a notice. It said, our dog is this color, this form. Whoever tells where he is, we will give him a thousand dollars. It had been put in the newspaper, and put in many places. They were very sad. I went, and I was very happy, but I did not show my happiness. The poor people were in separation. The dog had not been found. But Sri Krishna is the Lord. Without anyone telling him, without anyone asking him, he knows at once. All of this was done by Vidhi. Brahma has done it all. When Vidhi has done it, why should we forbid it. He quietly let it be.

2
00:02:00,020 --> 00:08:19,540
Then Krishna, to give joy to their mothers and to Brahma, made himself both. The maker of the makers, the Lord. In the previous verse Shukadeva had called him the knower of the universe. Now he says, the Lord who makes the universe. He is the Lord of those who create the world. The greatest creator. Everything is Krishna. What did he do. When he understood that Brahma had stolen both, in order to please the mothers, and to please Brahma too, he made himself into those calves and those boys. Exactly as they had been. As many calves as there were, as many cowherd friends, as their bodies were small or large, whatever color they were. There were thousands of kinds of calves. Some white, some black, some red. Ear, face, whatever there was, he became according to that. The stick, its color, its shape, its length, its thickness. The horn, the flute, the decoration of leaves. The same cloth, the same ornament. The same character, the same qualities, the same name, the same form, the same age. The same play, the same taste in eating. All of it was Vishnu. The thread at the waist, the cap, the lunch basket, the way of meeting the mother, of singing, of laughing, of asking for something. He became like that. He became the cowherds, and he became the calves. Nothing there was other than Vishnu. The Veda calls this world full of Vishnu, but this world is a transformation of the Lord's energy. Here, in those forms, the Lord himself appeared. We will not say transformed. The unborn Krishna, in every form, was very beautiful. Saying yavat once would have been enough.

3
00:08:20,020 --> 00:15:24,540
But there was no difference in each one either. So a year later, when Brahma looks with attention, the same calves and the same boys are playing with Krishna, eating, going into the forest, coming back. Where he had hidden them, they are still lying. He comes at great speed on the swan and looks. Here also it is the same. Which is true, which is new, which is the second. No difference appears, because yavat was said here. At that time every calf and every boy began to appear as Vishnu. Krishna alone, in all these forms. This lila will be told later. The hint here is the weight of the word yavat. Cloth, whatever there was, all became the Lord. Who is the person who can hear this event and still not accept Sri Krishna as the Lord. Is anyone able to make a lost man become the same man again. Whoever calls himself God, tell him, become two forms. Become the animal and become the man, exactly the same. There is no one. The Lord made no separate effort. No laboratory, no manufacture. He did not give birth to them. He did not sit and plan that it should happen so. Vidhi is the son. If his work is to steal, what can we do. We look after our own work. The Lord did not even quarrel. He simply expanded himself. In this way the Lord himself is also grazing the grass of Braj. The Lord in person grazes the grass here. This is the glory of this mandala. The word yavat has come again and again. What the Veda says, that all is full of Vishnu, became complete here, joined to the limbs. In what is conscious there are two truths, the living being and Vishnu. Here all of it is Vishnu. Today those boys are not the boys. Into every house Lord Krishna is entering as the calf and as the child. He himself became the calves and the herders. Surrounding himself with himself, gathering himself from here and there, he took them into Braj. The calves are the same, the boys are the same, and as Sri Krishna he is already the whole. Playing with himself, the soul of all entered Braj. Speaking, walking, playing, jumping. Driving himself with himself, he went into Braj.

4
00:15:25,410 --> 00:22:38,170
Taking each calf separately, he put each into its own pen. The calves of whichever house, himself, by himself, separated. In Bhojpuri there is a good word, higrana, to separate them out. The calves used to return about three or four o'clock. They grazed nearby, and the stomach filled quickly. They had to come before the cows. Run and put them in the stall. The boys go and tie the calf to the post, put down grass, meet the mother. Whatever the work was, they began to do that. No house was mistaken. He did not go as two into a house that had one boy. As they had been, so he entered. Love for her own child welled up in the mother. Whether she knew or not. The child coming into the house today is the Supreme himself, the treasure of bliss. The child who came home playing the flute was not an ordinary child. Without their knowing, an ocean of bliss welled up in the mothers' hearts. The mothers rose at once on hearing the sound of the flute. Today's rising was of another kind. A great eagerness. Hearing the flute, they got up immediately. Coming out of the house, they lifted the child with both hands and took him in the lap. The boys are five years old by now. But today's boys are Sri Krishna. So milk began to flow from the breasts. There were mothers whose breasts no longer gave milk. Today, even in the dry breasts, a stream of milk. Without their knowing, bliss rose toward the Lord. The heart was not getting full. Because of affection, milk flowed from the breast. What kind of milk. Like nectar. Really it was the milk of love. Taking the Supreme as their own son, they began to nurse him. A special nursing began today, and it went on for a year. Brahma did well, he really did take them. Every mother's wish was fulfilled. They had wanted Krishna to drink their milk, to become their son. The Lord honored their devotion, their affection, in this way.

5
00:22:38,170 --> 00:32:28,990
After that they take their own children into the house, put oil, put the bathing paste, bathe them, feed them, ornaments, and protection. They put the tilak, so the child would stay safe. He who makes and holds the whole world, who protects all, who blesses all, the root of every auspiciousness in the singing of whose name, those mothers were protecting that Lord. Service, with affection. Even the husband of Lakshmi, receiving the service of those mothers, counted himself fortunate. One meaning of yama is a watch, three hours. One meaning is also the time before evening, between noon and dusk. By that rule. The rule of coming home after noon. By that, Madhava came home every day. Every day the mothers lifted Sri Krishna in the same way and gave him milk. The Lord is hungry for love. First the milk, then the rubbing with oil. They knew the child was tired from herding the calves. Oil, then the midday bath. A good paste. They put on the ornaments. Protection, and tilak. Protection by the custom of the people, and also by the Vedic way. By a mantra, by Vishnu's mantra. May the Lord protect you so. Mothers keep a great worry. The folk protection, the black tilak, so that the evil glance ends. Somewhere they set a broken pot or a clay pot and wave it. That is a folk way, not the Veda. Lampblack in the eye. The point is that with great motherly love, with the love of the heart, the mothers were serving. Food also. Every day, putting them to sleep, singing. Here the verb is singular. One Krishna is being fondled in every place. Where the boys had been friends, Krishna was in those forms, so the singular. Fondled, moving among them, delighted. He learned to say Maiya, and Bhaiya. Balarama as brother, Nanda Baba as Baba, mother as Maiya. These three words the Lord, guru of the Vedas, of the devotees, and of Brahma, learned first. Surdas wrote it. Mohan began to say Maiya, Maiya. Nanda the chief as Baba, Baba. And Haladhara as brother. Do not go far to play, dear one, someone's cow will strike you. Cowherd men and women all make a happy noise. In every house the birth-music is playing. Surdas says, a sacrifice to your sight, a sacrifice to your feet. From his saying Maiya, Maiya, Yashoda says, my son, the life is successful. He will not be mute. He is learning to speak. He gave this happiness, in vatsalya, to all the gopis of Braj. He really became the son. Bathing, oil, feeding, nursing, fondling, care, the kiss. Madhava, though the husband of Lakshmi, accepted this affection. This is the good fortune of the mothers.

6
00:32:31,850 --> 00:38:56,560
Now the cows. The cows came quickly to the pen, calling. Called by the sound of the lowing, each began to nurse her own calf, licking again and again, the milk flowing from the udder. The cows were going and lowing, as they call for their own child. Today, without their knowing, an affection that cannot be told was welling in the heart. More than on other days. When they lowed, the children's voices were coming from the other side. The calves were answering the mother's word of affection. They were lowing too. They met. She was nursing her own calf, licking again and again, and giving the milk that flowed from the udder. There were cows whose second calf had been born after a year. Still they began to lick these children, and to give the milk that was flowing by itself. The Lord is giving good fortune to the cows. As a cowherd friend he was already drinking their milk, and now, becoming the calf, he is drinking it directly. This is the wonderful affection of Braj, more than one can hold. A question comes. Was the motherly feeling not there in the mothers before. It was. The gopis and the cows already had affection for Krishna. I am Krishna's mother. That feeling was in the gopis of vatsalya, and in the cows too. But that fullness of affection was not there. It was not the affection that says, Krishna is especially my son. Today's flood was not there. Now the relation of son has happened, so the affection grew. The Lord's feeling also was that the cows are my mother, and these gopis of vatsalya are also my mother. The motherly feeling was there, but today's possessiveness, that this is my mother, was not complete before. When he became the child, the feeling became full. From before, the gopis and the cows felt that this is my son, and the Lord felt that I am their son. But today's flood of affection was not there.

7
00:39:07,840 --> 00:43:11,770
Now this special event is happening. Slowly the people of Braj came to love their own son as much as they loved Krishna. It is astonishing. Why would it not grow. They are Krishna himself, become the son. When will Balarama know this. Every day he also herded the calves, he also came. When five or six days remained of the year, he thought, why is everyone loving their own children like this. Krishna is the highest love, the ground of happiness and bliss. Everyone's love was in Krishna, and it was there then too. But why is love for their own children growing equal to the love for Krishna. The Lord had laid such a bewilderment that for so many days he could not know. The Lord did not want him to know. When five days remained, one day he asked Krishna. Why is the love of the people of Braj, and of the cows, for their own children growing like their love for you. The Lord laughed. I myself have become all of them. Balarama, astonished, why did you not tell me before. You would have put an obstacle. You would have been angry at Brahma. That is why I did not tell. The affection of the people of Braj, of the cows, of the mothers, like a creeper, day and night, was growing day by day. For as long as the Lord has been obtained as the son. It grew as much as it had been in Krishna. Or, this flood is new even beyond what had been in Krishna before. Krishna is the whole, the source of the avatars. In this way, herding himself with himself, the lila of himself. For one year the Lord played.

8
00:43:13,490 --> 00:49:04,280
It is the story of one time. How the affection grew, Shukadeva Goswami is telling by one event. The cows were grazing on Govardhana. Once the unborn Sri Krishna was herding the calves, and five or six nights remained of the year. The year was not yet complete. Only five nights left. Sri Krishna was herding the calves, with Balarama. There is no separate talk of the ones he himself had become, because no one was there besides Krishna. Krishna himself was there as thousands of cowherds. The cows were grazing on the peak of Govardhana. While herding the children he took them a little near Govardhana. The cows saw their own children. By nature a cow's love is like that. They broke into a run from Govardhana. The cowherds, trying to stop them, were defeated. They came and began to nurse the children. The herd of cows, the bulls and the rest who were in the group, on seeing their own children, were under the power of affection. They forgot the grazing. They forgot even the awareness of the body. The cowherds thought, we will milk them, but if they go to the calves the milk will be finished. They began to stop them with sticks. Whatever happened. The cows had already gone past the cowherds who tended them. There was no stopping. It looked as if they were running on two feet. Tail up. The hump. They had no awareness of where the foot was falling, whether they would fall in a ditch. They were running only in affection for the children. This is the relation of the living being with the Lord. All the children were the Lord in person. Those whose calves were new, they also ran, and those who had only one calf ran even more. Coming, they were licking in such a way that it seemed they would swallow them. And they began to give their own milk.

9
00:49:04,280 --> 00:55:44,800
The cowherds became very angry, seeing this breaking of the rule by the cows. They had gone so fast in affection that the cowherds were left trying to stop them. From the uselessness of that effort, shame and anger. They ran hard from behind, we will not let them give the milk. Until now the cows had stayed in discipline. When they were driven home, they came. Today they have run in, outside the discipline. A beautiful principle should be understood here. If the living being's relation with the Lord happens, then one day, even if someone stops him, he does not stop. Here the cows are present in person, and those children are the Lord. The cowherds also became hard to approach, and angry. They were thinking, why did you bring the children over here. We will scold them, or give one slap. Anger at the cows. But what was their condition after they arrived. The moment those cowherds saw their own children, they went, lifted them with both hands, put them in the lap, and tears of love began to fall. They kept them in the lap a long time. By the sight, by the rasa of love that had risen, their whole intent was overcome. A wonderful love in the heart. Anuraga, the fifth ground of love, rose at that time. The anger left. Some began to smell the head. The highest bliss. The cows were nursing and licking, and the cowherds also held them in the lap. Shukadeva Goswami had felt one lack. The good fortune of the mothers had been described. The good fortune of the elder cowherds had not. They had gone there to beat the cows and scold the children. There, taking the children in the lap, tears of bliss. The cowherds who were grazing the cows, the elders, who had sober knowledge, who had discrimination, they also became fully satisfied by embracing their own children. With great difficulty they separated. Then they said, take these children far. The cows had to graze apart, the calves had to be taken on. Continuously the memory of their own child was there. The speaking, the walking, the touch, was coming in experience. In this way the Lord gave happiness to all the people of Braj. If they knew one should not be attached to the child of the family, then he in whom a man or a yogi wants to be attached, after leaving all the attachment of the world, that one has come as the son. Attachment to the son became the highest. The word entry is suggesting it. For a year the Lord gave himself. This is called the gift of himself. Falling under the power of the devotees' love, he gives himself. Hare Krishna.

10
00:56:39,190 --> 01:02:26,890
When, in this way, for a continuous year, the love of the mothers of Braj, of the cowherds, of the cows, of all the people of Braj, for their own sons, especially for the calves and for the cowherd boys, was growing. A growth of love. Because of that growth, a stretching of the throat. The longing stayed, when will we meet those children, when will we give milk, when will we serve. The movement of the mind was always running toward them. Utkantha. Ut means upward, kantha means the throat. Waiting for someone, to meet, to obtain a thing, a person keeps looking with the throat lifted. As there is a great longing that the train should come. The longing of the people of Braj was growing at every moment. What it is today, it grew tomorrow, it grew the day after. It was growing even after each moment. So much so that at the time of milking, the cows did not nurse their own children with as much love as they nursed the children who had grown up, the children who were Krishna. The breast given freely. They licked with great love and gave milk. The children who had grown, who no longer drank the mother's milk, love for them was also growing. At every moment. While living in the house, while thinking, everyone's mind stayed only on those children. When will we meet, when will we embrace, when will we give milk. Balarama saw this condition. He did not know the cause. It was a special quality of the Lord's lila, that he did not let Balarama know. If Balarama had known that the friends, Sridama, Madhumangala, and the others, had been stolen, he would have been very unhappy. Another thing, he could even have struck Brahma. Coming in anger. He is Shesha. Such a thing has been done, so he gives the rod. The lila would break. Some dryness would arise. He would scold, why did you do all this. And if Brahma had not done so, how would the Lord have given this kind of happiness to the people of Braj. So he did not let him know. The godhood that has been given. Krishna himself is in that form. The root is Krishna, the source of the avatars. He does not want Balarama to know, so Balarama could not know. The second body of Krishna, the second expansion. Even Rama could not know. What Krishna wants, that alone happens.

11
01:02:28,270 --> 01:07:32,070
So he began to think. For many days he thought. One day the worry grew more. What is this wonder I am seeing. As much love as the people of Braj had for Vasudeva, for the soul of all, for Sri Krishna, that same love is growing for their own children also. The word toka is for the calves and for the boys. Whose maya is this, what power is it. Directly. Balarama also saw that his own love for those children was growing. As much love as he had for Krishna, that much for those children. Seen with a clear eye, this maya was growing. For longing to grow in this way is maya. Balarama thinks, my love also is growing for these people, as it is for Krishna. Why is this happening. What maya is this. By the word maya he means, whose is this astonishing power that lays bewilderment, that lays confusion. Who is making us lovers of these children. No magic has been worked. The brother has worked it, and he does not know. Love for worldly people, and an attraction as great as for the Lord, this is a thing to think about. For the people of Braj, or for Balarama. Is this a divine maya. Of Brahma, of Shiva, of some god. Or a demoniac one. Not the maya of some demon. Another's maya can lay bewilderment on the people of Braj. It is bewildering me also. This maya should not be taken as the ordinary maya of the world. An astonishing power. This is some special quality of Sri Krishna himself, that my love also is growing for these children. Not a bewilderment from someone else's maya. Balarama is coming to the right decision. This is Krishna's own energy, his own wish, his own plan. Then this much love is growing in my mind.

12
01:07:34,840 --> 01:10:03,470
Even before, Balarama had come onto the cause. What is the cause that my mind is loving these children. With the eye of knowledge. Vayuna means knowledge. He began to consider with the eye of knowledge. He is the all-knowing Lord, so earlier he was not paying attention. Now he paid attention, and he understood at once. All the children appeared to him as Vaikuntha, as Sri Krishna. With a little attention. All of them. And the word api here means also. Not only the children. The clothes of the children, the decoration, whatever there was, he saw all of that as Vishnu, as Krishna. That is why my attraction is happening. The love of the people of Braj is also growing toward these. But why Krishna had become so many Krishnas, that he had not yet known. Why he had manifested himself in such a number. That he was not understanding.

13
01:10:03,470 --> 01:16:16,540
These are not the lords of the gods, nor are they sages. You alone are shining, even while resting in what looks different. You are all of them, each one separate. Say it in brief. Thus addressed, the Lord told what had happened. Balarama knew. Balarama began to ask Lord Sri Krishna. The two brothers were sitting. O Lord, this wonder is appearing here. All the friends there are, and the calves, these are not the best of the gods. Balarama knows that some best devotees among the gods had become calves, and some sages. Most are the Lord's eternal dear companions, but some gods and some sages had become cowherd boys and calves. Balarama saw, not one of these is a god, nor a sage. You alone are shining. O Lord, you alone are in every form. I have seen it. Even while resting in difference. They look like a different form, like Subala, Madhumangala, or the calves, different from you. But in form after different form, you alone are appearing. No one else is here. You are every separate one. Besides you there is nothing. Say it in brief. How is it that you have become all these forms. You have manifested yourself as the calves and as the herders. Nigama means in brief. Say it shortly. Tell the main hint. Are you playing a drama. When this was said, the Lord, Sri Krishna who is able to do all, told Balarama the whole thing. Now only five nights remained for the year to be complete. Balarama also became pleased. Right, Brahma did well. Or, inspiring Brahma, you yourself had it done. Balarama was laughing a great deal. Why did you not tell at the beginning. The mood of sweetness comes, so he asks, all right, it is no matter. One acharya says, this is the way to obtain divine knowledge. One should not keep the pride that I am the elder brother, I am the greater person, so why should I ask. He makes a comparison. Brahma once fell into confusion, it will be told ahead, but he did not ask the Lord. A small person thinks, I am the knower. He neither asks nor hears. Great people ask. Brahma did not ask, so he fell into many circles. Here the difference is shown. Balarama knew. The confusion that had come, the Lord removed. What was the confusion. Affection for those children. That had actually grown in Krishna. It was not confusion. As darkness cannot be imagined inside the circle of the sun, so ignorance is not possible in Balarama. That his affection should grow in someone other than Krishna, that does not happen.

14
01:16:18,970 --> 01:19:33,540
In this world, from time without beginning, the living being keeps searching for two things. One, the search for the beloved. The other, the search for bliss. Every living being wants bliss, and makes someone or other beloved. In the world they want that we should have someone who loves us. Because the soul's supreme beloved has an eternal relation with Krishna. So, by another road, he is searching for Krishna alone. He is waiting for him, in whatever body. And really, if he loves a living being, that also has become love for Krishna. How. The living being is also a part of Krishna. The day that living being leaves the body, we no longer love that body. We take it and put it in the ground, or burn it on the pyre. However dear the person, once the soul has left, that body does not remain dear. When the Lord is there in his own form of eternity, knowledge, and bliss, complete, how dear he will be can be understood easily. When one very fine, negligible part of his, coming into this body, was raising dearness of this kind. Balarama's conduct is the evidence. Love was growing in this way. The Lord is the Supersoul, the highest. Every living being is searching for the beloved, and wants happiness, wants bliss. Sri Krishna is condensed bliss. Bliss and nothing but bliss. In the Lord there is nothing else. By another road, the living being is wanting Sri Krishna, who is dense bliss. But he is wanting it out of foolishness. He does not know that happiness is not here, the Lord is not here. From this passage, the love of the people of Braj for their own children, and Balarama's love for them, the Lord's being dense bliss, his being the form of happiness, and his being the Supersoul, all of this is being shown.

15
01:19:35,460 --> 01:26:19,640
Now the talk of Brahma's confusion. Meanwhile the self-born one came. By his own measure, a truti. He saw Hari playing with all of them, as before, for a year. Here in Braj one year passed. How much time passed for Brahma. By his own measure. A truti. A truti means the time it takes for a fine needle to pierce the leaf of a lotus. That much time passed for Brahma, in his own mind. Our one year. This is called a truti. Three trutis make one pala. How long does it take to pierce a lotus leaf. The piercing takes no time. Removing the hand takes time. A mere truti is a sign that very little time passed. Brahma took the children away over there. He put the children to sleep and came here to see what further charming glory Krishna was showing. He saw the same boys and calves playing with Krishna. The calves grazing, the boys playing. Not one was less. Not one calf was missing, nor had a cowherd friend decreased. Size and kind, all complete. He saw Krishna playing with the calves and with the cowherds. Brahma thought, perhaps Krishna has picked them all up and brought them. He went and looked over there. As many calves and boys as there are in Gokula, all are asleep on the bed of his maya. They have not yet risen. Then where have these ones here come from. Here in Vrindavan, where did these come from. Where did those children come from. He began to count. He is a great scholar. As many as he had put to sleep, he counted and saw. Exactly the same. Form and the rest, the same. That many, playing together with Vishnu. They go, they sleep, they play again. No. These are not those children. Those calves and boys are asleep by my maya. Thinking for a long time on the difference between these. Atmabhu. Atma means the Lord, and bhu means birth. His birth is directly from the Lord. Even being so great, Brahma could not recognize. He considers, which is the real one. I stole the completely original ones and kept them there, and these also look exactly like that. A drop of truth. Which is true, which is not true. He was not able to know it in any way. However hard he tried, however he concentrated the mind, he could not become able to know. He had gone to see a charming glory. Now the heart began to pound. I have offended the Lord greatly. He is seeing a very beautiful glory, but he has fallen into the tangle, which is the true one, which is the copy. He thought by logic. He was seeing both sides completely the same.

16
01:26:20,220 --> 01:30:37,740
Thus, he who bewilders the universe, himself free of bewilderment, the bewilderer of the world, was bewildered by his own maya. Which is true, which is false. In this test Brahma became bewildered by his own maya. Now he himself cannot understand, so how will he bewilder the Lord. Here Lord Sri Krishna is called the one without bewilderment, and the bewilderer of the universe. Vimoha means the one in whom there is no confusion. In the Lord there is no confusion at all. As there is no darkness near the sun, no question of night. So there is no confusion in the Lord. He is all-knowing, all-powerful. But the bewilderer of the universe. He has laid the whole universe in confusion. The whole world is in confusion by the Lord's maya. But he cannot come into the circle of anyone's maya. He himself is free of confusion, and able to lay the universe in confusion. Brahma had gone to lay such a Vishnu, Sri Krishna, in confusion. He had laid him, he thought. The Lord who was searching for the calves had fallen into confusion, he thought. Brahma thought, let me see how he weeps, how he searches. This is what he wanted to see. But the Lord had become them himself. He did not weep. And if Brahma had not actually come this way to look, had not come to offer praise, the Lord would have remained so for endless time. Brahma's birth is not an ordinary birth. But by his own maya he himself is bewildered. By his own doing. Now he has fallen into the circle. Alas, why did I do this. Now what shall I do. Here he is called Vishnu. He became bewildered by his own maya. Shukadeva Goswami gives two examples of how Brahma's power could not work on the Lord. Darkness born of fog, against a darkness. You will have seen, when fog falls in the day, a kind of darkness forms. That is called the darkness of fog. Fog spreads at night also, and sometimes in the day. A thing filled with darkness, only darkness, dense. A night full of darkness. What effect will darkness born of fog have on that. What further darkness will it make. It cannot increase that darkness, and it cannot end that darkness. Darkness made of mist cannot put its effect on a night that is already dark. In that night one cannot even tell whether the fog is there. When the moon rises, then at night one can tell that fog is falling. Otherwise it is a dense night. One example has been given. The sitting stops here.
